// Title: Potential RjvPlatform.DLL Sideloading From Non-Default Location
// Sigma ID: 0e0bc253-07ed-43f1-816d-e1b220fe8971
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "RjvPlatform.dll" by "SystemResetPlatform.exe" located in a
//   non-default location.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1666716511988330499
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_rjvplatform_non_default_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\RjvPlatform.dll" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "\\SystemResetPlatform.exe") and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\SystemResetPlatform\\"))
